description: IR domain package — named kinds, no Svelte or vendor types
globs: src/lib/ir/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

# IR domain (`ir/`)

- `ir/` holds **named IR kinds**. The current UI-definition aggregate is **`UIDefinition`**. Do **not** introduce a type or file named `IRDefinition` / `ir-definition`.
- Treat breaking changes to a kind’s durable fields as high-risk. An additive field needs no migration step. A non-additive snapshot or IR shape change uses a versioned transform for that kind. Snapshot product versions under `versions/` are a different mechanism. Do not put a second migration path inside `UIDefinition`.
- `UIDefinition` public surface is `meta` / `components` plus operations (`append`, `loadSnapshot`, …). Do not add per-field get/set for live meta keys.
- Plugin projection views (e.g. map by `logicalId`) are not IR. Do not persist them on the snapshot or import adapter types here.
- Keep this package free of external UI-framework types, file I/O, and Svelte.
- UI-definition meta **DTO projections** (live / editor / snapshot / vendor export) live in `ui-definition-meta.ts`.
- Concrete UI kinds belong under `src/lib/ir/elements/`. Factories may return plain objects until a `Component` class hierarchy exists.
- `UIDefinition` aggregates elements; it does not know about Reader/Writer/Raw schemas or `ImportedDefinition`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — domain-only
export class UIDefinition { ... }

// ❌ BAD — framework leak into IR
import type { SomethingFromVendorSdk } from 'vendor-ui';

// ❌ BAD — catch-all kind name
export class IRDefinition { ... }
```
